# Git push
When the user says "push update" (or similar): stage and commit all relevant changes. The agent cannot run `git push` (no GitHub credentials in this environment). After committing, reply in one line that they should run `git push` locally—do not repeat long explanations.

# Links and navigation (CRITICAL — has caused 20+ hours of rework across athlete bios, Blue, admin profiles, States, etc.)
- **BLOCKER:** Links fail when (1) `<Link>` or `router.push()` is used inside Radix (DropdownMenu, Sheet, Dialog) — Radix intercepts the click; (2) same-site routes use `target="_blank"` — new tab often loads blank. Fix: use `<a href="...">` inside Radix; never `target="_blank"` for app routes.
- **Same rule everywhere:** Nav, dropdowns, athlete cards, admin tables, Blue page, NCHSAA/States, view-profile — if it’s an in-app route, follow this.
- **Inside Radix (dropdown, sheet, dialog):** Use plain `<a href="...">` only. Never `<Link>` and never `router.push()` alone. Radix intercepts and blocks navigation otherwise. Pattern: `<DropdownMenuItem asChild><a href={href}>...</a></DropdownMenuItem>`.
- **Never `target="_blank"` for same-site routes** (e.g. `/nchsaa/2026`, `/blue`, `/view-profile?id=...`). New-tab opens a blank or stuck page and has caused repeated “page never loads” issues. Use same-tab navigation unless the product explicitly requires “open in new tab” for that one link.
- **Before adding or changing any link:** (1) Use `<a href="...">` when inside a Radix menu/sheet. (2) Do not add `target="_blank"` for app routes. (3) Confirm the route exists. (4) Copy the pattern from a known working link in this codebase.
- **New pages:** Create the route first, then add the link using the same pattern as working items.

# New page returns 404 / links do nothing
- **Critical:** Critical links (Store, admin, new pages) must be plain `<a href="...">` (HardLink or StoreNavLink use real anchors) so navigation works with zero JavaScript.
- **404 in new tab but other pages (e.g. /blue) work:** Only some routes 404 = either (1) the deployment marked "Production" is not the latest (so new routes exist only on a newer deployment). **Fix:** Vercel → Deployments → find the deployment from the latest commit → ⋮ → "Promote to Production". (2) Or those routes throw at build time and get dropped — check Build logs for errors mentioning admin/orders or store. (3) Or they throw at runtime — check Function/Runtime logs when requesting that URL.
- **Redeploy with cache cleared:** Deployments → Redeploy → enable "Clear build cache" if the build might be stale.

# Adding a new page (REQUIRED — nav links have failed 7+ times; follow exactly)
- **Why:** New pages and new links often don’t work with client-side navigation — existing client bundles can have a stale route manifest, so RSC fetches get canceled. Full page load hits the server and works.
- **Step 1:** Create the route: `app/[your-path]/page.tsx` (e.g. `app/store/page.tsx` → `/store`).
- **Step 2:** For **any new internal link** (nav, footer, in-page): use **HardLink** (or StoreNavLink for `/store`) so navigation is a full page load. Import from `@/components/hard-link` or `@/components/store-nav-link`. Example: `<HardLink href="/your-path" className={...}>Label</HardLink>`. For navbar mobile with sheet: `<HardLink href="/your-path" className={...} onNavigate={() => setIsOpen(false)}>Label</HardLink>`.
- **Navbar:** Add the link using HardLink (or the existing `<a href="..." onClick={e => { e.preventDefault(); window.location.href = "..." }}>` pattern). Do **not** use `<Link>` or `router.push()` for new (or critical) internal links — they can fail for new routes.

# NHSCA (national placements — primary tournament focus)
- **Scope:** When the user says NHSCA / nationals / placements / `nhsca_placements`, work **NHSCA only**. Do not pivot to **Super32** or NCHSAA unless they ask or the error is explicitly in that API/column.
- **Single merge:** `getNHSCAForAthlete` in `lib/public-profile-data.ts` (re-export `@/lib/athlete-nhsca`). Do not add a second NHSCA merge path.
- **Same tournament year, multiple divisions:** NHSCA can have multiple rows per calendar year (e.g. Senior vs Junior brackets). Bracket pick is `dedupeNhscaByYearForGradYear` in `lib/tournament-tables.ts` using **grad year − tournament year** + division text. Multi-year history (2024 vs 2025) is not the same bug as same-year dedupe.
- **Postgres column names:** `athletes.super32_results` exists; **`athletes.super_32_results` does not** — a wrong `SELECT` breaks `/api/public-rankings` with `42703`. Verify column names against Supabase before assuming snake_case.
- **Server debug:** `RECRUITNC_DEBUG=1` or `RECRUITNC_DEBUG_NHSCA=1` — see `lib/recruitnc-debug.ts`. Client: `?debug=1` on profile URLs — see `lib/recruitnc-debug-client.ts`.

# Spartan / Fayetteville public athlete names (REGRESSION GUARD)
- **Public tables** (`/spartan`, `/api/spartan/supporters`, admin CSV exports) must show **roster `fullName`** from `fundraisingCodeToFullNameMap` when the NCU code matches; otherwise deterministic `fallbackAthleteLabelFromCode` — **not** Stripe checkout `athlete_display_name` (abbreviations like `M. Adams '27`).
- **Do not** reintroduce **Stripe hint** or session `athlete_display_name` paths in `resolvePublicAthleteCreditLabel` / `resolveFundraisingAthleteRowName` for those surfaces — that overrides merged roster names with checkout copy.
- **Do not** restore naive `seen.has(e.code)` merge for extras: use **`mergeFundraisingAthleteEntries`** in `lib/spartan-fundraising-code.ts` (case-normalized code, **prefer richer `fullName`**).
- **Before merging** changes to those modules: run `npm run test -- lib/spartan-fundraising-display.test.ts`. If you remove tested behavior, **update tests in the same PR**; dropping tests to green is not OK.

# Profile match data horizontal scroll (REGRESSION GUARD)
- **Wide tables** on `/view-profile` and `/unified-profile` must use **`ProfileScrollTable`** (`components/profile-scroll-table.tsx`) — never shadcn **`Table`** in `match-data-section-improved.tsx` (double scroll wrapper breaks iOS swipe).
- **Never** put `overflow-hidden` on the match-data card shell (`profileMatchDataCardClass` in `lib/profile-table-scroll.ts`).
- **Never** restore `table { display: block }` in `globals.css` or `touch-pan-x`-only on `scrollTableXClass`.
- **Before merging** changes to match data scroll, globals touch rules, or `ProfileScrollTable`: run `npm run test -- lib/profile-table-scroll.test.ts`.

# Debugging (F12)
- Errors are logged with the **[RecruitNC]** prefix so they’re easy to find in the browser console. When something breaks, copy the F12 console output (especially lines starting with [RecruitNC]) and paste it; the agent will fix from the actual error instead of guessing.

# Scripts that need to be run
- When adding or referencing any script that the user must run (e.g. SQL in Supabase SQL Editor, migrations, one-off commands), **always show the full runnable script in the chat** in addition to (or instead of) only putting it in a file. That way the user can copy and run it immediately without opening the file.

# Stripe webhook / shared env (Blue, Store, national team, drop-ins, etc.)
- **Reference:** See `docs/STRIPE-ENV-AND-FLOWS.md` for which env vars affect which flows (store, Blue, NHSCA/national team, drop-ins) and which support multiple values.
- **Before recommending any change to `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (or other env used by multiple flows):** Assume multiple Stripe destinations or endpoints may send to the same URL (Blue-Subscription, Store, national team, etc.). Recommending "set to X" can break other flows that use a different signing secret.
- **Always:** For webhook secret, recommend adding the new secret to the existing value (comma-separated) or listing all required secrets, not replacing. Example: "Add this destination’s secret to STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET; if you already have another (e.g. Store), use comma-separated: whsec_A,whsec_B."
- **Other Stripe env:** `STRIPE_BLUE_PRICE_ID` only affects Blue; `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` is one per account (all flows). Only `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` has "multiple secrets, one env" — use comma-separated.
- **Docs and error hints:** When documenting webhook setup or returning errors about invalid signature, mention that multiple secrets are supported (comma-separated) so one env update doesn’t break other parts of the platform.

# Tournament of Champions — public marketing page (`/tournament-of-champions`)
- **Tone:** Fan/athlete marketing only. Sell the tournament: *Who is #1*, elite competition, college exposure, premier venue (Hope Community Church, Apex), entertaining & competitive weekend, earn the Champion jacket.
- **Never on the public landing page:** Internal P&L, spectator counts/capacity (~350/~450/~500), inventory caps, ticket tier pricing tables (until product explicitly wants prices live), mat-throughput math, ops runbooks, or build-spec “success metrics.” Those belong in admin, Stripe, or internal docs — not `/tournament-of-champions`.
- **Schedule on page:** Fan-facing “when to be there” times are fine; omit buffer notes and operational contingency copy.
- **Build spec vs marketing:** Internal build spec may reference attendance targets and Stripe caps — do not mirror that language on the public page.
